was a construction worker before russia  invaded ukraine  when the war started he volunteered as a  civilian evacuation driver  he is now  missing feared dead  this video shows him after he had  rescued civilians from the besieged town  of pophasna  in the east of the country  igor was his co-driver on that day he  says sergey told him if he could save  another 20 people his life would not be  in vain  i could see the entrance to papasna  russian soldiers suddenly jumped out  from the left it happened so fast they  fired a rocket-propelled grenade but it  missed then they started shooting  machine guns and rifles  the windows shattered sergey kept  driving but he was hit and began falling  dragging the steering wheel to the left  we veered off the road crashing through  small trees  i was crouched down pushing up against  the dashboard i looked at sergey and he  wasn't moving or making any sound  i reached for the door handle jumped out  and started running between the trees  using the bus as cover  they continued shooting at it when i got  to a village i found a house and got  water i was covered in blood my face my  hands and ears i thought it was mine but  i had no wounds i realized then it was  it's not known exactly how many people  are either trapped inside porpuzna or  unwilling to leave a town that is under  near constant russian army attack  is volunteer evacuation driver mikhail  pankov having a blindfold taken off on  russian state tv  two days after he disappeared while also  trying to evacuate people trapped in  pophasna only civilians are doing the  evacuation he tells the man in military  uniform interviewing him  his daughter made an emotional plea on  facebook for his release  i beg you please giving my father back  we miss him so much please release him  let him go  in a village neighboring pophasna the  sound of artillery crashes through the  air  volunteers helena and yuri inspect the  graves where they have been burying  civilians killed in the besieged town  long trenches have been dug in which  bodies lie covered in soil  a tractor will fill in the trench when  the shelling dies down  there is more danger the shells can land  on you here it is over our heads we bury  them here because it's impossible to  bury them under the shelling it's too  dangerous to go in and collect the  bodies now  i feel great pity for people killed  if they're alive now they could be doing  something good it's very hard to  comprehend when you find a young person  lying dead on the ground  ukrainian authorities say dna testing  will be done when the war ends to  identify the growing number of  unidentifiable civilians killed  this is one of three unidentified graves  in this graveyard all that's written  on the cross is that a woman's body is  buried here  and the place where that body was found  for now the fighting in popular rages on  making it too dangerous for rescuing the  living or the dead  john stratford al jazeera rubika eastern  ukraine
 

